    "reviewed_findings": [
      "README, tier, formula, RAW, compatibility, source-index, and all four variant pages are internally consistent. The group has mixed melee/ranged kind, four real variants, and nine actual mark bindings.",
      "All four tiers replace the weakspot stagger-reduction multiplier with 0.4/0.3/0.2/0.1 after the mandatory finesse 0.5 reduction, corresponding to 60/70/80/90 percent less reduction relative to that weakspot baseline. The example treats R=50 as a raw input, not 50 percent: 50*0.5=25, then 10/7.5/5/2.5. Its stated no-extra-reduction (including burning), non-ignore profile, and no target weakspot override premises are explicit; it does not claim a final stagger or health-damage percentage.",
      "All four wrappers retain conditional ranged_impact_modifier +0.3, but only actual ranged attack_type consumers read that input. The formal text limits this to held Autogun P3 and Infantry Lasgun ranged attacks and says the input continues through power, armor, target, and stagger-count curves; the neutral-baseline 1.00+0.30=1.30 example is correctly scoped.",
      "The action coverage distinguishes pure push (push type and torso hit zone), push follow-up attacks, Powermaul direct/special profiles and interval ticks, Autogun bayonet/stock profiles, and the non-damaging Lasgun flashlight toggle. It preserves the native ignore-stagger-reduction and target weakspot-override branches.",
      "The blessing is described as a held conditional stat, with no proc stacks, cooldown, or timer. Equip installation, cache-delayed deactivation/reactivation on slot changes, and removal only on actual unequip are stated without promising same-frame cache updates.",
      "The exact bilingual RAW strings and paired SHA are preserved. Static formatter outputs are +60/+70/+80/+90 for weakspot and +30 ranged; the comparison correctly distinguishes visible formatted values from the runtime weakspot-reduction and ranged-impact inputs, classifying omitted runtime conditions as not covered.",
      "The UI receipt confirms the nine current labels and trait bindings: Shock Maul Agni Mk Ia and Munitorum Mk III; Arbites Shock Maul Branx Mk III; Vigilant Autogun Columnus Mk III, Graia Mk VII, Agripinaa Mk IX; Infantry Lasgun Kantrael Mk VII, Mk IIb, Mk IX. The Lasgun P2 metadata-only candidate is listed outside the actual binding set and is not included in the formal pages or map.",
      "The map has mixed kind, four matching variants and nine matching bindings; all four reverse weapon pages link back to the correct variant. Icon path weapon_trait_020 and the README attachment match the accepted image receipt.",
      "The latest preview 008 and current focused receipts are complete; focused source checks report 77 ranges/35 files, global map consistency, zero new link errors, and GFM checks passed. The fixed scope itself and all 80 listed files were hash-verified with Windows long-path handling."
    ],
